WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.245
Anthropic's sales grew more than

00:00:02.045 --> 00:00:03.840
thirteen times in a year,

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:04.837
and now it wants to

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:05.635
list on Nasdaq.

00:00:06.335 --> 00:00:08.692
First-half revenue was sixteen point

00:00:08.492 --> 00:00:10.222
three billion dollars,

00:00:10.022 --> 00:00:11.544
up from about one point

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.144
two billion a year earlier.

00:00:13.694 --> 00:00:15.822
The eighty point seven billion

00:00:15.622 --> 00:00:17.305
dollar loss is mostly a

00:00:17.105 --> 00:00:18.640
non-cash paper charge.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.295
The operating loss was six

00:00:20.095 --> 00:00:22.095
hundred ninety-three million,

00:00:21.895 --> 00:00:23.767
down from two point one billion.

00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:26.223
The seven co-founders hold one

00:00:26.023 --> 00:00:27.724
share with fifty point one

00:00:27.524 --> 00:00:28.816
percent of the vote.

00:00:28.856 --> 00:00:30.429
A trust elects most of

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:31.007
the board.

00:00:31.047 --> 00:00:32.784
Public buyers get money,

00:00:32.584 --> 00:00:33.453
not control.

00:00:34.003 --> 00:00:35.821
The day after the filing,

00:00:35.621 --> 00:00:37.581
banks and Blackstone lined up

00:00:37.381 --> 00:00:40.044
sixty-three billion dollars for Broadcom

00:00:39.844 --> 00:00:41.663
chips to lease to Anthropic.

00:00:42.213 --> 00:00:44.058
More than eleven thousand nine

00:00:43.858 --> 00:00:45.956
hundred customers spend a hundred

00:00:45.756 --> 00:00:47.664
thousand dollars a year or more.

00:00:47.704 --> 00:00:49.591
About nineteen hundred spend a

00:00:49.391 --> 00:00:50.403
million or more.

00:00:50.443 --> 00:00:51.745
The top five bring in

00:00:51.545 --> 00:00:53.236
about a quarter of revenue.

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:56.112
Enforcement is getting stricter,

00:00:55.912 --> 00:00:57.963
so gray-market keys and reseller

00:00:57.763 --> 00:00:58.923
seats can vanish.

00:00:58.963 --> 00:01:00.560
Move to a direct plan,

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.489
and read the risk factors yourself.

00:01:03.039 --> 00:01:04.613
The listing could come as

00:01:04.413 --> 00:01:06.119
soon as mid to late November.

00:01:06.159 --> 00:01:08.041
After that, a frontier lab

00:01:07.841 --> 00:01:10.666
reports to public shareholders every quarter.

00:01:11.216 --> 00:01:12.412
The full story,

00:01:12.212 --> 00:01:14.007
with what changes for Claude

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:15.866
developers, is on The Dispatch.

